      "text": "1 . The short url should be  unique and upto 5 -7 chars",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1 . The short url should be  unique and upto 5 -7 chars",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "RewbS1RTzUyXVxdsFB_vg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3157.8961199978808,
      "y": 264.77328204892433,
      "width": 1017.0384521484375,
      "height": 513,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1978042682,
      "version": 735,
      "versionNonce": 606089510,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1776507621137,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approaches:\n\n1. Use last 5 characters of each long urls\n    - security concerns\n    - predictable\n    - collision\n\n2.  base62 encoding\n        -use random number generator and encode it to base62\n        - still chances of collision\n        - can retry 2- 3 times of collision\n\n3. Use counter and give each upcoming url the next count (optimal)\n    hashed to base62 for compact representation \n   \n    1B urls - 10^9 in base62 - 6 characters \n    we have space to accomodate 62^ 6 = trillions urls can be accomodated in 6 digits so we have good scalability\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approaches:\n\n1. Use last 5 characters of each long urls\n    - security concerns\n    - predictable\n    - collision\n\n2.  base62 encoding\n        -use random number generator and encode it to base62\n        - still chances of collision\n        - can retry 2- 3 times of collision\n\n3. Use counter and give each upcoming url the next count (optimal)\n    hashed to base62 for compact representation \n   \n    1B urls - 10^9 in base62 - 6 characters \n    we have space to accomodate 62^ 6 = trillions urls can be accomodated in 6 digits so we have good scalability\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "pdXTqL8gFw_6dMIZlEvKB",
