    {
      "id": "vLBod8yZgbKRN97vBZi6z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2183.0350622882056,
      "y": 1520.448022712657,
      "width": 430.5595703125,
      "height": 135,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ai",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 680380134,
      "version": 543,
      "versionNonce": 1740968954,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1776507576532,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Total Space Approx:\n\n1 row in url  - 500B\n500 * 10 ^ 9 = 10 ^ 11 B = 500 GB  (so a single\nDB instance is sufficeint for this scale)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Total Space Approx:\n\n1 row in url  - 500B\n500 * 10 ^ 9 = 10 ^ 11 B = 500 GB  (so a single\nDB instance is sufficeint for this scale)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "mkPk0ldH5iNTVajcqkjxM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 856.1302748007495,
      "y": 1400.8248673134117,
      "width": 1053.6185302734375,
      "height": 513,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "al",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 459374758,
      "version": 1110,
      "versionNonce": 1303379494,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1776506139481,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep Dives :\n\n1. How will you handle scale upto 100M DAU and 1B records of  URLs\n    \n    As suppose each row is 500B at max a database needs here is 500 GB which is supported by single standard ssd\n    \n    Suppose we have 100M active user - 100K writes per day - 1 write per second \n   \n    Also the system is  read heavy so we could potentially seperate out read service which will only handle redirection\nand write service which will handle url creation\nThey can both scale independently based on the demand . But if we want to scale out write service to maintain\nconsistency we need to maintain global counter in redis \n\n\nWhat about HA ?\n    - redis supports HA modes which \n     - also postgres db can be configured with replica with postgres async repliaction to support HA\n    \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep Dives :\n\n1. How will you handle scale upto 100M DAU and 1B records of  URLs\n    \n    As suppose each row is 500B at max a database needs here is 500 GB which is supported by single standard ssd\n    \n    Suppose we have 100M active user - 100K writes per day - 1 write per second \n   \n    Also the system is  read heavy so we could potentially seperate out read service which will only handle redirection\nand write service which will handle url creation\nThey can both scale independently based on the demand . But if we want to scale out write service to maintain\nconsistency we need to maintain global counter in redis \n\n\nWhat about HA ?\n    - redis supports HA modes which \n     - also postgres db can be configured with replica with postgres async repliaction to support HA\n    \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
